From: zaken9090 <zaken9090@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lavender-1026: AMP again (gold A73 = P cluster, silver A53 = E cluster), as topaz-0141 had it

XNU boots on the gold cluster now (1003) and can run all eight cores (ADT --all8). Without
__ARM_AMP__ the scheduler saw one homogeneous cluster and put the window server's render thread
on a 1.37 GHz A53 as often as on a 2.2 GHz A73: eight cores were slower than four in Settings.
With it, threads of the default and higher QoS go to P, background/utility and kernel threads
to E (recommended_pset_type() without CLPC), and P spills to E only when it is busy.
Without an E cluster (four gold cores) pcores_recommended() no longer touches the NULL
ecore_set, and kernel threads stay on P (the display driver copies CPU-rendered frames).
The ADT marks the cores 'P' / 'E' (mkadt_lavender.py --all8).

---

diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
@@ -43,8 +43,7 @@
  * silver A53 = E cluster (ADT cluster-type). The Edge scheduler then keeps
  * threads on P and spills to E only when P is busy (no CLPC recommends).
  */
-/* lavender: XNU boots on the silver A53 cluster only (gold runs at 1/4
- * clock, see lavender/dump probes); one homogeneous cluster, no AMP. */
+#define __ARM_AMP__               1
 #endif
 
 #define HAS_GIC_V3                1
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/processor.c b/osfmk/kern/processor.c
index aad9f3b..fae1089 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/processor.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/processor.c
@@ -1682,9 +1682,16 @@ recommended_pset_type(thread_t thread)
 	switch (recommendation) {
 	case CLUSTER_TYPE_SMP:
 	default:
+#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
 		if (get_threadtask(thread) == kernel_task) {
 			return PSET_AMP_E;
 		}
+#endif
+		/*
+		 * lavender: kernel threads stay on P too. The display driver copies every frame
+		 * the CPU renders (10 MB) and the HID/USB/GPU work loops run there; on a 1.37 GHz
+		 * A53 that made eight cores slower than four.
+		 */
 		return PSET_AMP_P;
 	case CLUSTER_TYPE_E:
 		return PSET_AMP_E;
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/sched_amp.c b/osfmk/kern/sched_amp.c
index 93b6512..cc00755 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/sched_amp.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/sched_amp.c
@@ -618,6 +618,11 @@ pcores_recommended(thread_t thread)
 		return false;
 	}
 
+	if (!ecore_set) {
+		/* lavender: no E cluster (four gold cores only): everything runs on P */
+		return true;
+	}
+
 	if (pcore_set->online_processor_count == 0) {
 		/* No pcores available */
 		return false;
